[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186157296 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" "question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" "question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/id #uuid "ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-83488" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c8c3764dcdd63bb7f7078ccdb729a95712f788db25fc1ba048172fc06b2b3d1.png)\n\nFind the total area bounded by the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we want to find the interval for $\\theta$ that corresponds to the first petal. Since the curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $3\\theta \\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n3\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSo, the first petal is traversed for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](images/75/75e6fabf01bb0a73e17efee8d9d52d7c1e66cfd78eccd3d5c4d1f9e087335c1f.png)\n\nSince there are $3$ petals, the total area bounded by the polar curve can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{total}} & =3\\cdot {A}_{\\text{petal}} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{(\\theta +\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ))|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/id #uuid "daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106" "answer-0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6" "answer-d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a" "answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" "answer-65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106" :answer/id #uuid "08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6" :answer/id #uuid "0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a" :answer/id #uuid "d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" :answer/id #uuid "ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46" :answer/id #uuid "65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157297 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" "question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/id #uuid "bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/math-academy-id "q-83524" :question/problem "![](images/53/53d86dd26966e3e4b5a75441fc7a1d6ab8f2244097f61677086f5783495ed6cb.png)\n\nThe area of one loop of the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )$ is given by the integral\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhich of the following represents the total area bounded by the polar curve?" :question/worked-solution "The given polar curve is the polar rose with $5$ petals, and we know that the area of the first petal is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n![](images/53/53d86dd26966e3e4b5a75441fc7a1d6ab8f2244097f61677086f5783495ed6cb.png)\n\nThe $1$st petal is traversed from ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ to ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{5},$ and the length of this interval is $\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo find the interval for the second petal, we have to add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the first petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{3} & ={\\theta }_{1}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=0+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{4} & ={\\theta }_{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to obtain the interval for the third petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the second petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{5} & ={\\theta }_{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{6} & ={\\theta }_{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the interval for the fourth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the third petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{7} & ={\\theta }_{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{8} & ={\\theta }_{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the interval for the fifth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the fourth petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{9} & ={\\theta }_{7}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{4\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{10} & ={\\theta }_{8}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we obtain the following intervals for all $5$ petals of our rose:\n\n$$\n{{[0,\\frac{\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{1\\text{st}},\\,{{[\\frac{\\pi }{5},\\frac{2\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{nd}},\\,{{[\\frac{2\\pi }{5},\\frac{3\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{rd}},\\,{{[\\frac{3\\pi }{5},\\frac{4\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{th}},\\,{{[\\frac{4\\pi }{5},\\pi ]}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{th}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total area of the given polar curve can be obtained if the curve is traversed from $\\theta =0$ to $\\theta =\\pi :$\n\n$$\n{A}_{\\text{total}}=\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7" "answer-981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c" "answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" "answer-26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4" "answer-a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7" :answer/id #uuid "897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{2\\pi /5}^{3\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c" :answer/id #uuid "981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{4\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" :answer/id #uuid "ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4" :answer/id #uuid "26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6" :answer/id #uuid "a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /5}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/id #uuid "1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-86387" :question/problem "![](images/98/984b29e4fa91543e74b6dec14794d2c46175633ab1118a67246e015055177182.png)\n\nFind the total area bounded by the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we want to find the interval for $\\theta$ that corresponds to the first petal. Since the curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $5\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ]$:\n\n$$\n5\\theta =0,\\pi \\,⟹\\,\\theta =0,\\frac{\\pi }{5}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the first petal is traversed for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{5}.$\n\n![](images/e4/e41fe5bc79759e102339e1824d82691c45fb454a86b1ca4674b1d6ba5770c107.png)\n\nSince there are $5$ petals, the total area bounded by the polar curve can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{total}} & =5\\cdot {A}_{\\text{petal}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}{(\\theta -\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\theta ))|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}[(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" :answer-field/choices ["answer-804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d" "answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" "answer-3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26" "answer-7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b" "answer-355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d" :answer/id #uuid "804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" :answer/id #uuid "e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26" :answer/id #uuid "3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b" :answer/id #uuid "7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9" :answer/id #uuid "355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/id #uuid "177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/math-academy-id "q-86398" :question/problem "![](images/42/4219b3046fc4911823e18f42cf911c39ae2a41bc9b3e8fe56839339ed3caabcb.png)\n\nThe area of one loop of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ (shown above) is given by the integral\n\n$$\nA=2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhich of the following represents the total area bounded by the polar curve?" :question/worked-solution "The given polar curve is the polar rose with $5$ petals, and we know that the area of the first petal is\n\n$$\nA=2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nThe $1$st petal is traversed from ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{20}$ to ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{20},$ and the length of this interval is $\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo find the interval for the second petal, we have to add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the first petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{3} & ={\\theta }_{1}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{20} \\\\ {\\theta }_{4} & ={\\theta }_{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to obtain the interval for the third petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the second petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{5} & ={\\theta }_{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\theta }_{6} & ={\\theta }_{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the interval for the fourth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the third petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{7} & ={\\theta }_{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20} \\\\ {\\theta }_{8} & ={\\theta }_{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{13\\pi }{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the interval for the fifth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the fourth petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{9} & ={\\theta }_{7}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{13\\pi }{20} \\\\ {\\theta }_{10} & ={\\theta }_{8}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{13\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{17\\pi }{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we obtain the following intervals for all $5$ petals of our rose:\n\n$$\n{{[-\\frac{3\\pi }{20},\\frac{\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{1\\text{st}},\\,{{[\\frac{\\pi }{20},\\frac{\\pi }{4}]}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{nd}},\\,{{[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{9\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{rd}},\\,{{[\\frac{9\\pi }{20},\\frac{13\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{th}},\\,{{[\\frac{13\\pi }{20},\\frac{17\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{th}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total area of the given polar curve can be obtained if the curve is traversed from $\\theta =-\\frac{3\\pi }{10}$ to $\\theta =\\frac{17\\pi }{20}:$\n\n$$\n{A}_{\\text{total}}=2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{17\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" "answer-80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e" "answer-fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127" "answer-0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0" "answer-faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" :answer/id #uuid "f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{17\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e" :answer/id #uuid "80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{9\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127" :answer/id #uuid "fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /20}^{13\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0" :answer/id #uuid "0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{17\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f" :answer/id #uuid "faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /10}^{\\pi /10}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/id #uuid "b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-125054" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f25a56285499e3b2547e68bc57d4bbac3d79282c669f56e41d74de3394cb89c3.png)\n\nFind the total area bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we want to find the interval for $\\theta$ that corresponds to the first petal. Since the curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )=0.\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $2\\theta \\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n2\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the first petal is traversed for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](images/6b/6b70070505112ec0f12749b64937e3e0a8e8f72d77bfc1966a3edfb4c03c16b5.png)\n\nSince there are $4$ petals, the total area bounded by the polar curve can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{total}} & =4\\cdot {A}_{\\text{petal}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =18\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =9{(\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta ))|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =9[(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))] \\\\  & =9(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd" "answer-4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef" "answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" "answer-a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852" "answer-3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd" :answer/id #uuid "1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef" :answer/id #uuid "4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" :answer/id #uuid "554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852" :answer/id #uuid "a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb" :answer/id #uuid "3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a07fb17c-ba96-5327-8cfb-559571f3e84b" :activity/id #uuid "a07fb17c-ba96-5327-8cfb-559571f3e84b" :activity/title "The Total Area Bounded by a Single Polar Curve" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049711 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968" "step-83876909-484d-5098-9056-cda5b61077b2" "step-2a827fa0-f523-550d-a1f9-61848c5a518a" "step-e4918b9d-c94f-534e-a5b6-37da54630b83" "step-12b6f6ed-ca53-5abb-a74c-097bf2234742"] :activity/first-step "step-eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968" :step/id #uuid "eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968" :step/content "question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :step/next "step-83876909-484d-5098-9056-cda5b61077b2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-83876909-484d-5098-9056-cda5b61077b2" :step/id #uuid "83876909-484d-5098-9056-cda5b61077b2" :step/content "question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :step/next "step-2a827fa0-f523-550d-a1f9-61848c5a518a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2a827fa0-f523-550d-a1f9-61848c5a518a" :step/id #uuid "2a827fa0-f523-550d-a1f9-61848c5a518a" :step/content "question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :step/next "step-e4918b9d-c94f-534e-a5b6-37da54630b83" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e4918b9d-c94f-534e-a5b6-37da54630b83" :step/id #uuid "e4918b9d-c94f-534e-a5b6-37da54630b83" :step/content "question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :step/next "step-12b6f6ed-ca53-5abb-a74c-097bf2234742" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-12b6f6ed-ca53-5abb-a74c-097bf2234742" :step/id #uuid "12b6f6ed-ca53-5abb-a74c-097bf2234742" :step/content "question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/id #uuid "ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9"] ["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-83488"] ["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c8c3764dcdd63bb7f7078ccdb729a95712f788db25fc1ba048172fc06b2b3d1.png)\n\nFind the total area bounded by the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$ shown above."] ["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/worked-solution "First, we want to find the interval for $\\theta$ that corresponds to the first petal. Since the curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $3\\theta \\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n3\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSo, the first petal is traversed for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](images/75/75e6fabf01bb0a73e17efee8d9d52d7c1e66cfd78eccd3d5c4d1f9e087335c1f.png)\n\nSince there are $3$ petals, the total area bounded by the polar curve can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{total}} & =3\\cdot {A}_{\\text{petal}} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{(\\theta +\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ))|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/id #uuid "daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416"] ["answer-08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106" :answer/id #uuid "08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106"] ["answer-08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106" :answer/value "2\\pi"] ["answer-0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6" :answer/id #uuid "0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6"] ["answer-0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6" :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["answer-d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a" :answer/id #uuid "d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a"] ["answer-d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a" :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" :answer/id #uuid "ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd"] ["answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd" :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["answer-65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46" :answer/id #uuid "65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46"] ["answer-65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46" :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/correct "answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/choices "answer-08df229c-f083-5307-b9de-b175fb567106"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/choices "answer-0f6a0f59-5f8f-5623-9653-c39a8b989fe6"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/choices "answer-d8e063c4-ae33-50e6-8319-76861871384a"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/choices "answer-ecd25d64-1537-5f14-ac15-6043beb007dd"] ["answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416" :answer-field/choices "answer-65235364-004d-5570-a7e2-7a5a2d965f46"] ["question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-daa7ef23-6409-58fc-bb35-cb770de11416"] [17592186157296 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ffe58f3d-d1df-5f63-91ca-dbeff6b8e3f9"] ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/id #uuid "bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937"] ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/math-academy-id "q-83524"] ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/problem "![](images/53/53d86dd26966e3e4b5a75441fc7a1d6ab8f2244097f61677086f5783495ed6cb.png)\n\nThe area of one loop of the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )$ is given by the integral\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhich of the following represents the total area bounded by the polar curve?"] ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/worked-solution "The given polar curve is the polar rose with $5$ petals, and we know that the area of the first petal is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n![](images/53/53d86dd26966e3e4b5a75441fc7a1d6ab8f2244097f61677086f5783495ed6cb.png)\n\nThe $1$st petal is traversed from ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ to ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{5},$ and the length of this interval is $\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo find the interval for the second petal, we have to add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the first petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{3} & ={\\theta }_{1}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=0+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{4} & ={\\theta }_{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to obtain the interval for the third petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the second petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{5} & ={\\theta }_{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{6} & ={\\theta }_{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the interval for the fourth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the third petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{7} & ={\\theta }_{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{8} & ={\\theta }_{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the interval for the fifth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the fourth petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{9} & ={\\theta }_{7}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{4\\pi }{5} \\\\ {\\theta }_{10} & ={\\theta }_{8}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we obtain the following intervals for all $5$ petals of our rose:\n\n$$\n{{[0,\\frac{\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{1\\text{st}},\\,{{[\\frac{\\pi }{5},\\frac{2\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{nd}},\\,{{[\\frac{2\\pi }{5},\\frac{3\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{rd}},\\,{{[\\frac{3\\pi }{5},\\frac{4\\pi }{5}]}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{th}},\\,{{[\\frac{4\\pi }{5},\\pi ]}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{th}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total area of the given polar curve can be obtained if the curve is traversed from $\\theta =0$ to $\\theta =\\pi :$\n\n$$\n{A}_{\\text{total}}=\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta\n$$"] ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec"] ["answer-897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7" :answer/id #uuid "897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7"] ["answer-897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7" :answer/value "3{\\int }_{2\\pi /5}^{3\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c" :answer/id #uuid "981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c"] ["answer-981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{4\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" :answer/id #uuid "ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f"] ["answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4" :answer/id #uuid "26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4"] ["answer-26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6" :answer/id #uuid "a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6"] ["answer-a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /5}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/correct "answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/choices "answer-897536db-c849-5d79-9ba4-a4238f040ab7"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/choices "answer-981dbf45-34e1-59de-a03b-1dca1acd434c"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/choices "answer-ba8dcbb1-a6e1-5679-a9ff-a0be957e988f"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/choices "answer-26a670ea-427e-5238-9927-db5c6ee8c9b4"] ["answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec" :answer-field/choices "answer-a426a802-6c0d-511f-9aa5-03fc4b99fdb6"] ["question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a9d481e0-f5fc-5471-81ce-37fd48de7cec"] [17592186157297 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bbb22cb1-13ec-5d3b-bdb0-92451851f937"] ["question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/id #uuid "1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9"] ["question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-86387"] ["question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/problem "![](images/98/984b29e4fa91543e74b6dec14794d2c46175633ab1118a67246e015055177182.png)\n\nFind the total area bounded by the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ),$ shown above."] ["question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/worked-solution "First, we want to find the interval for $\\theta$ that corresponds to the first petal. Since the curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $5\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ]$:\n\n$$\n5\\theta =0,\\pi \\,⟹\\,\\theta =0,\\frac{\\pi }{5}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the first petal is traversed for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{5}.$\n\n![](images/e4/e41fe5bc79759e102339e1824d82691c45fb454a86b1ca4674b1d6ba5770c107.png)\n\nSince there are $5$ petals, the total area bounded by the polar curve can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{total}} & =5\\cdot {A}_{\\text{petal}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}{sin}^{2}⁡(5\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}{(\\theta -\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\theta ))|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}[(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2"] ["answer-804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d" :answer/id #uuid "804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d"] ["answer-804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d" :answer/value "3\\pi"] ["answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" :answer/id #uuid "e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23"] ["answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23" :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["answer-3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26" :answer/id #uuid "3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26"] ["answer-3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26" :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}"] ["answer-7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b" :answer/id #uuid "7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b"] ["answer-7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b" :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["answer-355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9" :answer/id #uuid "355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9"] ["answer-355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9" :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/correct "answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-804c522b-2546-5b42-b388-ed8f359d919d"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-e46e5fee-7c5f-594f-a2d1-b40e95316d23"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-3b967fc2-14ef-5591-ac47-05ea43361a26"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-7b6276de-d4ff-525f-aee1-fae9bf68d18b"] ["answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2" :answer-field/choices "answer-355e8a24-3e4d-57a5-861a-d745aa6c2ad9"] ["question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1311cc8a-7312-51de-a573-db9c65d763c2"] [17592186157296 :knowledge-point/questions "question-1d78e501-2778-5069-95a8-ae459e1095c9"] ["question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/id #uuid "177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475"] ["question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/math-academy-id "q-86398"] ["question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/problem "![](images/42/4219b3046fc4911823e18f42cf911c39ae2a41bc9b3e8fe56839339ed3caabcb.png)\n\nThe area of one loop of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ (shown above) is given by the integral\n\n$$\nA=2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhich of the following represents the total area bounded by the polar curve?"] ["question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/worked-solution "The given polar curve is the polar rose with $5$ petals, and we know that the area of the first petal is\n\n$$\nA=2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nThe $1$st petal is traversed from ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{20}$ to ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{20},$ and the length of this interval is $\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$\n\nTo find the interval for the second petal, we have to add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the first petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{3} & ={\\theta }_{1}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{20} \\\\ {\\theta }_{4} & ={\\theta }_{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to obtain the interval for the third petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the second petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{5} & ={\\theta }_{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\theta }_{6} & ={\\theta }_{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the interval for the fourth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the third petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{7} & ={\\theta }_{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20} \\\\ {\\theta }_{8} & ={\\theta }_{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{13\\pi }{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the interval for the fifth petal, we add $\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ to both ends of the interval of the fourth petal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{9} & ={\\theta }_{7}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{9\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{13\\pi }{20} \\\\ {\\theta }_{10} & ={\\theta }_{8}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{13\\pi }{20}+\\frac{\\pi }{5}=\\frac{17\\pi }{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we obtain the following intervals for all $5$ petals of our rose:\n\n$$\n{{[-\\frac{3\\pi }{20},\\frac{\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{1\\text{st}},\\,{{[\\frac{\\pi }{20},\\frac{\\pi }{4}]}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{nd}},\\,{{[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{9\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{rd}},\\,{{[\\frac{9\\pi }{20},\\frac{13\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{th}},\\,{{[\\frac{13\\pi }{20},\\frac{17\\pi }{20}]}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{th}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total area of the given polar curve can be obtained if the curve is traversed from $\\theta =-\\frac{3\\pi }{10}$ to $\\theta =\\frac{17\\pi }{20}:$\n\n$$\n{A}_{\\text{total}}=2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{17\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta\n$$"] ["question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee"] ["answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" :answer/id #uuid "f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d"] ["answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d" :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{17\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e" :answer/id #uuid "80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e"] ["answer-80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e" :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{9\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127" :answer/id #uuid "fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127"] ["answer-fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127" :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /20}^{13\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0" :answer/id #uuid "0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0"] ["answer-0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-3\\pi /20}^{17\\pi /20}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f" :answer/id #uuid "faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f"] ["answer-faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /10}^{\\pi /10}{cos}^{2}⁡(5\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/correct "answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/choices "answer-f8fae2a6-65b4-5042-9335-262d07b1045d"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/choices "answer-80f14876-6021-5bb8-ad9b-e903f9ca567e"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/choices "answer-fc32d924-2d20-5976-b132-c8852bba7127"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/choices "answer-0d117994-a925-5b34-82a3-8d5a3cb0eeb0"] ["answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee" :answer-field/choices "answer-faae2eaa-a25c-57e1-8d32-a1a21400e75f"] ["question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b90b688e-1cfc-5f16-b29a-74c4de3775ee"] [17592186157297 :knowledge-point/questions "question-177597c2-89ca-5fab-9eb3-c33a0eb21475"] ["question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/id #uuid "b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9"] ["question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-125054"] ["question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f25a56285499e3b2547e68bc57d4bbac3d79282c669f56e41d74de3394cb89c3.png)\n\nFind the total area bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ shown above."] ["question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/worked-solution "First, we want to find the interval for $\\theta$ that corresponds to the first petal. Since the curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )=0.\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $2\\theta \\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n2\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,⟹\\,\\theta =-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the first petal is traversed for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](images/6b/6b70070505112ec0f12749b64937e3e0a8e8f72d77bfc1966a3edfb4c03c16b5.png)\n\nSince there are $4$ petals, the total area bounded by the polar curve can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{total}} & =4\\cdot {A}_{\\text{petal}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =18\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =9{(\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta ))|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =9[(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))] \\\\  & =9(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3"] ["answer-1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd" :answer/id #uuid "1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd"] ["answer-1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd" :answer/value "18\\pi"] ["answer-4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef" :answer/id #uuid "4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef"] ["answer-4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef" :answer/value "9\\pi"] ["answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" :answer/id #uuid "554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679"] ["answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679" :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{2}"] ["answer-a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852" :answer/id #uuid "a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852"] ["answer-a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852" :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}"] ["answer-3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb" :answer/id #uuid "3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb"] ["answer-3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb" :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/correct "answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-1f7a34db-1ee5-5bbe-a2b7-4ba01e8c37fd"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-4d604b51-9113-53d1-afe3-1b6f2abc8bef"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-554965bc-836b-5822-aa80-8be991a21679"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-a84bdd1d-1d4e-5d1f-9068-b59e3aac2852"] ["answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3" :answer-field/choices "answer-3b7f9a8b-3eaa-5374-ac7e-bb44a97c8adb"] ["question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-46e620b9-37df-57d1-a0e4-42db20f457d3"] [17592186157296 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b6ddac46-46f7-5402-a079-ffa97b59c2f9"] ["activity-a07fb17c-ba96-5327-8cfb-559571f3e84b" :activity/id #uuid "a07fb17c-ba96-5327-8cfb-559571f3e84b"] ["step-eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968" :step/id #uuid "eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968"] ["step-83876909-484d-5098-9056-cda5b61077b2" :step/id #uuid "83876909-484d-5098-9056-cda5b61077b2"] ["step-2a827fa0-f523-550d-a1f9-61848c5a518a" :step/id #uuid "2a827fa0-f523-550d-a1f9-61848c5a518a"] ["step-e4918b9d-c94f-534e-a5b6-37da54630b83" :step/id #uuid "e4918b9d-c94f-534e-a5b6-37da54630b83"] ["step-12b6f6ed-ca53-5abb-a74c-097bf2234742" :step/id #uuid "12b6f6ed-ca53-5abb-a74c-097bf2234742"] ["step-eb9487ce-e2a6-5fc3-a245-3e17fc114968" :step/content "question-ffe58f3